  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration is config_006 (multimodal, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.542), which marginally outperforms RNA-only multiprofile (config_002, acc=0.530). However, all experiments so far have used avgpool as the sole aggregation method, and the multiprofile→singleprofile jump was the largest single improvement observed (0.41→0.53 for RNA). This means the aggregation strategy is a critical but unexplored design dimension. Question: Does transformer aggregation outperform avgpool for combining multiprofile representations in the multimodal setting with the best-performing encoders (scgpt + ViT-L)? Why this experiment: config_027 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer relative to config_006, isolating a single variable while building on the strongest existing configuration. If transformer aggregation improves performance, it reveals a new lever for further gains; if it does not, it confirms avgpool sufficiency and redirects search toward other dimensions (fusion, RNA encoder). This is the highest-information single-variable test available under the limited budget."
}

